1
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:49,333
Inspired by the actual files of Father Gabriele
Amorth, Chief Exorcist of the Vatican.

2
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:32,666
The Pope's Exorcist is a horror, thriller film directed by Julius Avery.

3
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Father Gabriele Amorth, Chief Exorcist of the Vatican, investigates a young boy's terrifying possession and
ends up uncovering a centuries-old conspiracy the Vatican has desperately tried to keep hidden.

4
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:59,333
Father Gabriele Amorth, played by Russell Crowe.

5
00:28:36,666 --> 00:28:42,666
Father Esquibel, played by Daniel Zovatto.

6
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Julia, played by Alex Essoe.

7
00:40:03,333 --> 00:40:09,333
Henry, played by Peter DeSouza-Feighoney.

8
00:45:46,666 --> 00:45:52,666
Asmodeus (voice), played by Ralph Ineson.

9
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Amy, played by Laurel Marsden.

10
00:57:13,333 --> 00:57:19,333
The Pope's Exorcist is a 2023 supernatural horror film directed by Julius Avery from a screenplay by Michael Petroni and Evan
Spiliotopoulos, based on the 1990 book An Exorcist Tells His Story and the 1992 book An Exorcist: More Stories by Father Gabriele Amorth.

11
01:02:56,666 --> 01:03:02,666
The film stars Russell Crowe as Amorth, with Daniel Zovatto,
Alex Essoe, and Franco Nero in supporting roles.

12
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:46,000
Production began in 2020 when Screen Gems
purchased the rights to Amorth's story.

13
01:14:23,333 --> 01:14:29,333
After a directorial replacement and script revisions, filming
occurred in Ireland from August to October 2022.

14
01:20:06,666 --> 01:20:12,666
The Pope's Exorcist was released in several  countries beginning on
April 5, 2023, and in the United States on April 14.

15
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:56,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $77 million worldwide.

16
01:31:33,333 --> 01:31:39,333
The film explores themes of spain, rome, italy, pig, vatican (holy see), pope.

17
01:37:16,666 --> 01:37:22,666
The tone is dark and intense.
